***Types of Docker Networks and Their Uses***

In Docker, different network types are used for different communication purposes.

1. Bridge Network
A private internal network for containers on the same Docker host.

Use:
Container-to-container communication
Most commonly used network
Default Docker network
Example
docker network create custom --driver bridge 
Use Case:

Frontend container communicating with backend container on same machine.

2. Host Network
Container directly uses the host machine’s network.

Use:
Better performance
No network isolation
Container shares host ports
Example
docker run --network host nginx
Use Case
Applications requiring high-speed networking.

3. None Network
Container has no network access.

Use
Maximum isolation
Security purposes
Testing environments

Example
docker run --network none ubuntu
Use Case

Running isolated secure containers.

4. Overlay Network
Connects containers running on multiple Docker hosts.

Use
Used in Docker Swarm
Multi-host container communication
Example
docker network create -d overlay myoverlay

